{"authored" [{"question" "q-280387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $H=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}],$ then $det(H)=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}|-7|\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-7(0-(-20))+2(-3-0) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot (20)+2\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-140-6 \\\\  & =-146\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "226750f8251e509be463671ba78f03a950cc0fee6988f2255a6404ddf708f85a" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280387" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280387" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-146"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $R=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ then $det(R)=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(3\\cdot 2-5\\cdot (-1))+2(4\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 6)+0 \\\\  & =1(6+5)+2(8-30) \\\\  & =11+2(-22) \\\\  & =11-44 \\\\  & =-33\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "226750f8251e509be463671ba78f03a950cc0fee6988f2255a6404ddf708f85a" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280394" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-280394" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-33"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $R$ given below?\n\n- $R$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(R)=0$\n- $det(R)=1$\n\n \n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{aligned}|-\\sqrt{2}|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(0+\\sqrt{2})-\\sqrt{2}(2+1)+2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 3+2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}-3\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(R)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "226750f8251e509be463671ba78f03a950cc0fee6988f2255a6404ddf708f85a" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/state.json" "file_sha256" "46d566ee65bb8b9943a7d958e0dc303130cb027fe97b73a3ddbe0e713676bcac" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/example-14762.json" "file_sha256" "98134812a30d155c701221a65f5480f7b75f9d6425c5ce2d002b9c4852e14599" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -12 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-3)|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0(8+96)+3(8+48)+6(-96+48) \\\\  & =0+3\\cdot 56+6\\cdot (-48) \\\\  & =168-288 \\\\  & =-120\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/example-14762.json" "file_sha256" "98134812a30d155c701221a65f5480f7b75f9d6425c5ce2d002b9c4852e14599" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $A$ given below?\n\n- $\\det(A) = 0$\n\n- $A$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n- $A$ is a singular matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/example-14763.json" "file_sha256" "769f9c3e23fde5efa65243b816f9924113c584fc25b7d3d03ba7cbe9e8104510" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(0-4)-2(7-3)+3(4-0) \\\\  & =-4-2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-4-8+12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/example-14763.json" "file_sha256" "769f9c3e23fde5efa65243b816f9924113c584fc25b7d3d03ba7cbe9e8104510" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the determinant of  $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ is $2,$ find the value of the constant $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/example-14764.json" "file_sha256" "05e9abb1d54b649d715a2304054673723b731aabb1c8f492f1bfab4f9b2c9b85" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-14764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(12-10)-1(3k-0)+2(2k-0) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3k+2\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =6-3k+4k \\\\  & =k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $2,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k+6 & =2 \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/example-14764.json" "file_sha256" "05e9abb1d54b649d715a2304054673723b731aabb1c8f492f1bfab4f9b2c9b85" "basis" 789 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974828/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $Q$ given below?\n\n- $Q$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $Q$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(Q)=-5$\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980449/state.json" "file_sha256" "bda94cd1eaec19467308085c550244439efa51a166194b2f26ae59eef20cda00" "basis" 868 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980449/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-3(8-14)+6(5-8) \\\\  & =0-3\\cdot (-6)+6\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =18-18 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(Q)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980449/state.json" "file_sha256" "bda94cd1eaec19467308085c550244439efa51a166194b2f26ae59eef20cda00" "basis" 868 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980449/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8896951a70b3c68de4b197a716eaaa1e89a0ab050bf47fc124b4a06e30124bfb" "basis" 868 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980449/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38182" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980449/state.json" "file_sha256" "bda94cd1eaec19467308085c550244439efa51a166194b2f26ae59eef20cda00" "basis" 868 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980449/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38182" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980449/state.json" "file_sha256" "bda94cd1eaec19467308085c550244439efa51a166194b2f26ae59eef20cda00" "basis" 868 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980449/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38182" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980449/state.json" "file_sha256" "bda94cd1eaec19467308085c550244439efa51a166194b2f26ae59eef20cda00" "basis" 868 "verification" "/home/jake/Develope